Fillets: patch 0980's concave crease (ChFi3d_ConcaveCreaseBeyond) judged
as the faces meet at the edge itself (mitcad#1341).

0980 lets the ball turn about a crease between a face and the next one,
taken for tangent (normals within a tenth of a radian), only where the
crease is concave. It asked ChFi3d::DefineConnectType with its point
correction on, which moves a point within a hundredth of an extruded or
B-spline face's parameter range of the range's bound that far into the
face. On the extrusion of a fin's profile spline that is 0.17 mm along the
spline, past which its normal had turned by more than the crease of 1.4
degrees between it and the arc's cylinder before it: the convex crease came
out concave, the ball rolled on its edge, which it leaves at once on a
convex crease, and the walk made one point and failed. The connection is
now judged at the edge itself, where the function checks the normals for
its angle already.

On a reported fin's top chamfered over slight creases and rounded with
0.2: the walk after each arc's torus passes onto the spline's top. Test:
geometry/tests/test_fillet_fin_top_creases.cpp (with patch 1301; without
this patch the rounding fails on both contours).

Upstream: new.

diff --git a/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKFillet/ChFi3d/ChFi3d_Builder_2.cxx b/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKFillet/ChFi3d/ChFi3d_Builder_2.cxx
index 29c22146..b4782b19 100644
--- a/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKFillet/ChFi3d/ChFi3d_Builder_2.cxx
+++ b/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKFillet/ChFi3d/ChFi3d_Builder_2.cxx
@@ -3574,7 +3574,11 @@ static bool ChFi3d_ConcaveCreaseBeyond(const TopoDS_Edge& E,
       return false;
     }
   }
-  return ChFi3d::DefineConnectType(E, F1, F2, 1.e-5, true) == ChFiDS_Concave;
+  // (Concave as the faces meet at the edge itself, not with the points moved
+  // off a face's parameter bounds: on a curved B-spline or extruded face that
+  // is a hundredth of its range into it, where across a crease of a degree or
+  // two its normal can lie on the other side of the other face's.)
+  return ChFi3d::DefineConnectType(E, F1, F2, 1.e-5, false) == ChFiDS_Concave;
 }
 
